{"status": "ok", "backend": "ddgs-auto", "query": "What drugs prevent incretin degradation at endothelium for diabetes treatment?", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T19:33:29.117914+00:00", "documents": [{"title": "Incretin Based Treatments - Diabetes Teaching Center", "url": "https://diabetesteachingcenter.ucsf.edu/about-diabetes/type-2-diabetes/medications-therapies-type-2-diabetes/incretin-based-treatments", "snippet": "Medications, called incretin based treatments, are available to control post-meal glucagon, and help reduce the post meal blood glucose. The incretin based medications are available in two families of medicines: DPP-4 Inhibitors and GLP-1 analogs."}, {"title": "Incretin-Based Therapies for the Treatment of Type 2 Diabetes ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2809297/", "snippet": "The two most recently approved classes of therapeutic agents for the treatment of type 2 diabetes, glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) receptor (GLP-1R) agonists and dipeptidyl peptidase-4 inhibitors (DPP-4i), exert their actions through potentiation of incretin receptor signaling."}, {"title": "Updates of incretin‐related drugs for the treatment of type 2 ...Targeting the incretin system in obesity and type 2 diabetes ...GLP-1 receptor agonists and atherosclerosis protection: the ...How DPP-4 Destroys Incretins and Why Inhibitors Block ItRewriting Diabetes Therapy: How Incretin Modulation is ...", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9889679/", "snippet": "Nov 14, 2022 · Among incretin‐related drugs, because the DPP‐4 inhibitors are effective to reduce HbA1c with little risk of hypoglycemia and are neutral to the bodyweight, they might be preferred for older patients with type 2 diabetes. Apr 17, 2024 · We review the latest advances in incretin-based pharmacotherapy. These include ‘GLP1 plus’ agents, which combine the known advantages of GLP1RAs with the activity of additional hormones, such as... Glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonists (GLP-1RAs) are incretin mimetics endorsed by major professional societies for improving glycemic status and reducing atherosclerotic risk in people living with type 2 diabetes. Mar 22, 2026 · Five DPP-4 inhibitors (sitagliptin, saxagliptin, linagliptin, alogliptin, and vildagliptin) are approved for type 2 diabetes treatment worldwide. They all work the same way: competitively or substrate-selectively inhibiting the DPP-4 catalytic site to prevent GLP-1 and GIP cleavage. Jan 5, 2026 · Pharmacological exploitation of the incretin axis gave rise to GLP-1 receptor agonists (GLP-1RA) and dipeptidyl-peptidase-4 inhibitors (DPP-4i), the latter preventing rapid enzymatic degradation of native incretins [7]."}]}
